      nPromoSub: 'On the night your Lantern Vessel fills to 10, tonight\'s spirits and works, with a story and music written by AI, become a 55-second video in the last room',
      nPromoMore: '✦ Bring a Gold Light or Silver Light spirit, and something special lights up the last room. What will happen on your night?',
      nRule1: 'Choose <em>7 spirits</em> from your catalogue. Their total radiance can be <em>up to {cap}</em>',
      nRule2: 'Walk the corridor and light <em>4 galleries behind doors, in order</em>. Inside, send <em>1 to 3 spirits</em>; if their total radiance reaches <em>the light it needs</em>, the gallery is lit. A spirit with an element the gallery <em>loves</em> gives <em>×1.2</em>. Spirits you send <em>rest</em> for the night. Door 3 opens with a <em>photo of a light</em> near you',
      nRule3: 'After 4 galleries comes the last corridor. The <em>Door of Light</em> opens without a key, and entering the last room brings <em>dawn</em>. Each gallery you light and each arrival in the last corridor adds 1 light to your <em>Lantern Vessel</em> (5 a night, so it fills in 2 nights). <em>Only on the night it fills to 10</em> is a <em>one-of-a-kind video</em> made in the last room. That night, choose 1 of the 7 spirits you brought and it becomes <em>tonight\'s guardian</em>. When no group can light a gallery, a <em>quiet morning</em> comes. <em>There is no losing</em>. Tonight\'s museum is set by the date, so <em>everyone gets the same night</em>',
      nRule4: 'Each lit gallery gives you <em>a frame</em>, and the <em>spirit and artwork</em> that lit it go inside (if 2 or 3 spirits lit it, you choose one; it can\'t be swapped later). <em>Light all 4 and the frames turn gold</em>. Frames hang in the last corridor and the last room',
      nRuleMore: 'The key photo for door 3 is <b>only checked on this device</b>: it is not sent to any AI and nothing is kept. In room 3, the key image covers <b>the walls of the room</b> for that night only. Your <b>Lantern Vessel</b> keeps the light from nights you stop partway and from retries (only on this device). On a night when it is full, the spirit you choose at the Door of Light becomes <b>tonight\'s guardian</b>: its figure and name appear beside the pillar of light in the last room\'s video, quietly watching over you (any spirit works the same; its Radiance does not change, and its catalogue card gets a guardian mark). If you go on without choosing, the video is made without a guardian. The vessel empties at the end of the night the video is made. On the night the vessel is full, in the last room a <b>55-second video</b> with music shows tonight\'s spirits and works lighting up, and you can save it (it is made on this device). At the end, the works and spirits slip out of their frames, circle the pillar of light as they gather, and rise through the skylight together with your photo and the guardian. The morning scene has 4 stages by how many galleries you lit. A Gold Light or Silver Light spirit at dawn adds a golden pillar / silver rain. In the last room, an AI looks at tonight\'s works and writes the story (captions and a title) and a plan for the music. Only the artwork numbers and the spirits\' names are sent (never a key image or your photo). <b>When the AI is available</b>, the title, the caption for each frame and the music are made for the spirits in tonight\'s 4 frames. <b>When it isn\'t</b> (the daily limit, a relay problem, etc.), the video plays with no captions and the usual title and music. Either way the video is made the same way and can be saved (the last room shows which one it is above "Into the light"). In the last room you can choose "Leave it to us" or "My image on the walls". You can use one image of your own, and it fills each wall between the pillars (it is used only on this device: not sent anywhere and not kept; it does appear in a video you save). In the last room, a Gold Light spirit\'s frame gets a golden pillar from the skylight and a Silver Light spirit gets silver rain, each with its own sound (strength doesn\'t change). You can put <b>your own photo</b> in the middle of the pillar of light (take one right there or use any photo you have; just one). “📷 Take one now” works with a computer webcam or a phone; the camera runs only while you take the photo and stops as soon as you close it. You can also take the photo of a light for the door 3 key the same way. It is used only on this device: not sent to any AI or to us, and not kept (it does appear in a video you save). If you close the page partway, you can pick up <b>on the same day with "Continue"</b>, in front of the next door (the spirits you brought, the galleries you lit and the frames you received are kept only on this device and are cleared when morning comes; key images and photos are not kept, so before door 3 you choose the photo again).',
